    "Each entry carries a CENTRE and an approximate RADIUS, not a real polygon.",
    "The seed turns those into a bounding box so every spatial query works on a",
    "laptop with no network and no OSM extract. They are deliberately coarse.",
    "",
    "`pnpm db:osm:ingest` replaces each of these boundaries with the real OSM",
    "polygon and stamps `osmId` on the row. The seed never overwrites a row that",
    "already carries an `osmId`, so re-seeding after an ingest cannot downgrade",
    "real boundaries back to boxes.",
    "",
    "Coordinates are [latitude, longitude] in WGS84."
